WEBVTT

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:01.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Builder.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Blueprint.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:04.074 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson one.

00:00:04.626 --> 00:00:05.355 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Introduction.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:07.616 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Education only.

00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:09.489 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:12.061 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information and

00:00:12.061 --> 00:00:14.264 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:16.164 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
financial situation or needs.

00:00:16.684 --> 00:00:18.448 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is high risk; you could

00:00:18.448 --> 00:00:20.139 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lose all the money you put in.

00:00:20.659 --> 00:00:22.724 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:22.724 --> 00:00:24.434 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
indicator of future results.

00:00:25.484 --> 00:00:27.540 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The prices are public historical

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.302 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily closes, marked Example.

00:00:29.822 --> 00:00:31.889 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A close is the last price of the day.

00:00:33.044 --> 00:00:34.943 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:00:35.942 --> 00:00:37.841 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end of this series you will

00:00:37.841 --> 00:00:40.076 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
understand what a grid bot does, when it

00:00:40.076 --> 00:00:42.310 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
can capture bounces, and where it loses.

00:00:42.772 --> 00:00:44.783 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will know how to plan one, test

00:00:44.783 --> 00:00:46.682 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it on paper, run it, check it, and

00:00:46.682 --> 00:00:48.730 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
change the capital you give to bots

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.591 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
only under written risk rules.

00:00:51.111 --> 00:00:52.508 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is education, not

00:00:52.508 --> 00:00:53.828 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a promise of results.

00:00:54.878 --> 00:00:56.219 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end you will know

00:00:56.219 --> 00:00:57.503 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
what a grid bot places.

00:00:58.633 --> 00:01:00.711 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will see that idea on

00:01:00.711 --> 00:01:02.686 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
one real path from 2023.

00:01:03.886 --> 00:01:05.395 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will be able to say the

00:01:05.395 --> 00:01:06.847 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop rule in one sentence.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.647 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
When a chart says Example, it

00:01:09.647 --> 00:01:11.493 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
means a real past price used

00:01:11.493 --> 00:01:13.339 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as an example, not a forecast.

00:01:14.389 --> 00:01:16.899 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is digital money, such as bitcoin.

00:01:17.419 --> 00:01:19.095 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not need to have bought

00:01:19.095 --> 00:01:20.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
any before this lesson.

00:01:20.758 --> 00:01:22.726 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange is the website or app

00:01:22.726 --> 00:01:25.058 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
where you swap Australian dollars for

00:01:25.058 --> 00:01:27.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto, and crypto back to dollars.

00:01:27.618 --> 00:01:29.294 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course does not name one,

00:01:29.294 --> 00:01:30.970 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and it does not send an order.

00:01:31.715 --> 00:01:33.280 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Cash is money you can spend.

00:01:33.682 --> 00:01:35.581 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here that means dollars, or a coin

00:01:35.581 --> 00:01:37.704 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that is meant to stay near one dollar.

00:01:38.011 --> 00:01:40.203 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Coin is the crypto, such as bitcoin.

00:01:41.253 --> 00:01:43.599 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order is an instruction to buy or sell.

00:01:44.051 --> 00:01:45.858 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A buy order swaps cash for coin.

00:01:46.378 --> 00:01:48.742 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A sell order swaps coin back to cash, and

00:01:48.742 --> 00:01:51.106 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you can only sell coin you already hold.

00:01:52.156 --> 00:01:53.926 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot is software that places

00:01:53.926 --> 00:01:55.548 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and refills orders for you.

00:01:56.068 --> 00:01:58.433 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid bot places waiting buy orders

00:01:58.433 --> 00:02:00.561 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on lines below the price and sell

00:02:00.561 --> 00:02:02.689 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
orders on lines above it, inside a

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.423 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
top and a bottom you choose.

00:02:04.943 --> 00:02:06.619 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The space between your top and

00:02:06.619 --> 00:02:08.351 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your bottom is called the band.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.566 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sells need some coin, so a grid

00:02:10.566 --> 00:02:12.515 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
starts with part cash and part

00:02:12.515 --> 00:02:14.465 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
coin, and that is a description,

00:02:14.465 --> 00:02:16.336 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not advice about what to hold.

00:02:17.386 --> 00:02:19.092 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A limit order is an order that

00:02:19.092 --> 00:02:20.656 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waits at a price you choose.

00:02:21.176 --> 00:02:22.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not chase the price.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.724 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Chasing the price would mean

00:02:24.724 --> 00:02:26.176 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
moving the order to follow

00:02:26.176 --> 00:02:27.741 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wherever the price has gone.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.665 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order fills when the price reaches

00:02:30.665 --> 00:02:32.397 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
its line and the trade happens.

00:02:32.858 --> 00:02:35.065 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Until then, the order is only waiting.

00:02:36.115 --> 00:02:38.070 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Think of a ladder leaned on a wall.

00:02:38.212 --> 00:02:40.558 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The rungs wait, and they do not chase you.

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:43.124 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A rung is one price where an order waits.

00:02:43.531 --> 00:02:45.710 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The gap is the space between two rungs.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.043 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The ladder is the analogy, and the

00:02:48.043 --> 00:02:50.315 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
chart beside it is the real past path.

00:02:51.365 --> 00:02:52.776 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The range is the top rung

00:02:52.776 --> 00:02:53.905 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the bottom rung.

00:02:54.425 --> 00:02:56.548 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The levels are the rungs between them.

00:02:56.897 --> 00:02:59.188 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop is the written rule for leaving.

00:03:00.037 --> 00:03:01.881 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The range is the top line and the

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.724 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom line, taken from the path.

00:03:04.203 --> 00:03:07.427 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The chart is bitcoin's real daily

00:03:07.427 --> 00:03:10.997 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closes from 19 July to 16 October 2023.

00:03:11.517 --> 00:03:12.969 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every close in this window

00:03:12.969 --> 00:03:14.701 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stayed between those two lines.

00:03:15.487 --> 00:03:18.079 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Six equal gaps of about 900 dollars sit

00:03:18.079 --> 00:03:20.752 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
between the bottom line and the top line.

00:03:21.272 --> 00:03:23.499 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each gap is about 900 dollars:

00:03:23.499 --> 00:03:25.726 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the top line minus the bottom

00:03:25.726 --> 00:03:27.210 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
line, divided by six.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.065 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is one step between

00:03:29.065 --> 00:03:30.549 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lines, not the whole band.

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:32.907 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Seven lines make those six gaps.

00:03:33.427 --> 00:03:35.215 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The levels are the prices on the

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:36.891 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
rungs where limit orders wait.

00:03:37.878 --> 00:03:40.168 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Buy orders wait on lines below the price.

00:03:40.604 --> 00:03:42.559 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Sell orders wait on lines above it.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:45.540 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each fill changes what you hold: a buy

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.206 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fill adds coin, and a sell fill adds cash.

00:03:48.726 --> 00:03:49.843 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You choose the band,

00:03:49.843 --> 00:03:51.128 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the gaps and the money.

00:03:51.412 --> 00:03:52.864 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The bot places each order.

00:03:53.871 --> 00:03:55.664 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
After a fill, the bot places the

00:03:55.664 --> 00:03:57.385 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
opposite order one rung away.

00:03:57.905 --> 00:04:00.083 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A buy fill gets a sell one rung higher.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.700 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A sell fill gets a buy one rung lower.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:04.840 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You still write the stop, and

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:06.516 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you act when that rule is met.

00:04:06.747 --> 00:04:08.982 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The bot does not decide the stop for you

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:11.105 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
unless you turned that setting on, and

00:04:11.105 --> 00:04:13.172 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you write which one before you start.

00:04:13.906 --> 00:04:15.247 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Think of a market stall.

00:04:15.679 --> 00:04:17.793 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stallholder buys stock a little

00:04:17.793 --> 00:04:19.907 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cheaper and sells it a little dearer,

00:04:19.907 --> 00:04:21.527 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and pays a fee on every sale.

00:04:21.978 --> 00:04:23.705 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid can do that while price

00:04:23.705 --> 00:04:25.145 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bounces inside the band.

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:28.186 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bounce means price moves down and back

00:04:28.186 --> 00:04:30.555 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
up, or up and back down, and stays inside.

00:04:31.075 --> 00:04:33.311 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One buy at a lower line and the later

00:04:33.311 --> 00:04:35.394 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sell of that same coin is one pair.

00:04:35.914 --> 00:04:38.247 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On these daily closes, the summer window

00:04:38.247 --> 00:04:40.651 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
finished only three pairs one rung apart.

00:04:41.171 --> 00:04:42.903 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sell line is higher, so the

00:04:42.903 --> 00:04:44.747 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cash that comes back is more than

00:04:44.747 --> 00:04:46.702 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the cash that left, before the fee.

00:04:46.995 --> 00:04:48.448 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A fee is what the exchange

00:04:48.448 --> 00:04:50.012 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
charges when an order fills.

00:04:50.193 --> 00:04:51.813 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The fee comes out of the gap.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:53.772 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the fees are larger than the

00:04:53.772 --> 00:04:55.336 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gap, the pair keeps nothing.

00:04:55.517 --> 00:04:56.760 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is not a promise.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.084 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair finishes only if price

00:04:59.084 --> 00:05:00.957 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
does bounce and both orders fill.

00:05:02.007 --> 00:05:03.236 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The daily close is the

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:04.465 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
last price of the day.

00:05:04.886 --> 00:05:06.686 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto trades all day, so the

00:05:06.686 --> 00:05:08.094 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
day is cut at a set time.

00:05:08.614 --> 00:05:11.138 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The daily close is the end of each

00:05:11.138 --> 00:05:13.569 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
UTC day, 11am in Sydney in summer.

00:05:14.089 --> 00:05:16.073 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is a simple candle that shows

00:05:16.073 --> 00:05:17.748 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the day's high, low and close.

00:05:18.222 --> 00:05:20.151 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Traders call it a candle because

00:05:20.151 --> 00:05:22.081 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the full version has a thick body

00:05:22.081 --> 00:05:23.813 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and a thin wick, like a candle.

00:05:24.244 --> 00:05:25.753 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here we only need the high,

00:05:25.753 --> 00:05:26.982 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the low and the close.

00:05:27.316 --> 00:05:30.495 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This candle is 19 July 2023.

00:05:31.015 --> 00:05:32.244 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The high, the low, and

00:05:32.244 --> 00:05:33.529 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the close are labelled.

00:05:34.422 --> 00:05:36.551 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The example is Bitcoin's public

00:05:36.551 --> 00:05:38.207 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily price in US dollars.

00:05:38.727 --> 00:05:41.926 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
From 19 July 2023 to 16 October

00:05:41.926 --> 00:05:44.869 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
2023, every one of those days

00:05:44.869 --> 00:05:47.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closed inside the band.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:49.493 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The close crossed the seven

00:05:49.493 --> 00:05:51.239 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lines 28 times in that window.

00:05:51.759 --> 00:05:54.071 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The count is an example, not a forecast.

00:05:54.591 --> 00:05:56.378 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
We do not need to read each day.

00:05:56.644 --> 00:05:57.987 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The shape is the lesson,

00:05:57.987 --> 00:05:59.401 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and it is marked Example.

00:05:59.921 --> 00:06:02.677 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Worked check: 19 July

00:06:02.677 --> 00:06:05.757 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
2023 to 16 October 2023.

00:06:06.277 --> 00:06:07.786 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The low is the bottom line.

00:06:08.266 --> 00:06:09.732 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The high is the top line.

00:06:10.252 --> 00:06:12.095 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Nothing on this card is an order.

00:06:13.059 --> 00:06:15.993 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Those 28 crossings are not 28 results.

00:06:16.513 --> 00:06:18.715 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A crossing only means the close moved

00:06:18.715 --> 00:06:20.782 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
from one side of a line to the other.

00:06:21.224 --> 00:06:22.935 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A pair is finished only when a

00:06:22.935 --> 00:06:24.789 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buy and its later sell have both

00:06:24.789 --> 00:06:26.521 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled, and only after the fee.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:28.920 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The price can cross many lines and

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.819 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
still leave you holding coin if it

00:06:30.819 --> 00:06:32.439 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
walks out through the bottom.

00:06:32.976 --> 00:06:35.957 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In this example a buy waiting at the

00:06:35.957 --> 00:06:39.246 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lower of these two lines was reached on

00:06:39.246 --> 00:06:42.227 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
17 August 2023, and the sell one line

00:06:42.227 --> 00:06:45.208 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
above was reached on 29 August 2023.

00:06:45.728 --> 00:06:47.516 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The card shows the gap, then the

00:06:47.516 --> 00:06:49.080 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
two fees, then what is left.

00:06:49.389 --> 00:06:51.512 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That is about eight and a half dollars

00:06:51.512 --> 00:06:53.244 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
after fees, for one small pair.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.540 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It happens only if the price comes

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:57.216 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
back up through the sell line.

00:06:57.320 --> 00:06:59.051 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the price leaves through the

00:06:59.051 --> 00:07:00.839 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom, you still hold the coin,

00:07:00.839 --> 00:07:02.403 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the pair never finishes.

00:07:02.595 --> 00:07:04.383 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This card is not money you made.

00:07:11.311 --> 00:07:13.099 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Now watch what you hold when the

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:15.110 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price leaves the band and stays out.

00:07:15.373 --> 00:07:16.994 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Above the band the sells have

00:07:16.994 --> 00:07:18.781 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled and you are holding cash,

00:07:18.781 --> 00:07:20.234 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with nothing left to sell.

00:07:20.638 --> 00:07:22.202 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Below the band the buys have

00:07:22.202 --> 00:07:23.655 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled and you are holding

00:07:23.655 --> 00:07:25.387 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
coin, with nothing left to buy.

00:07:25.669 --> 00:07:27.061 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That is why the way down

00:07:27.061 --> 00:07:28.820 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
matters most: every buy fills,

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:30.578 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you are left holding coin.

00:07:32.628 --> 00:07:34.863 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here is that stop rule on the real path.

00:07:35.283 --> 00:07:37.644 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It triggers if a daily close is outside

00:07:37.644 --> 00:07:39.931 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the band, through the top or the bottom,

00:07:39.931 --> 00:07:42.440 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still outside.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.412 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then the idea is finished.

00:07:44.792 --> 00:07:46.886 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You stop the bot, which cancels the

00:07:46.886 --> 00:07:48.755 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waiting orders, and do what you

00:07:48.755 --> 00:07:50.849 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wrote: keep the coin or swap to cash.

00:07:51.369 --> 00:07:53.351 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot's automatic stop is a price

00:07:53.351 --> 00:07:55.039 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that can fire during the day.

00:07:55.559 --> 00:07:57.258 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course uses the two daily

00:07:57.258 --> 00:07:59.094 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closes, unless your written plan

00:07:59.094 --> 00:08:00.882 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
says you turned on a price stop.

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:03.447 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On 23 October 2023 the close

00:08:03.447 --> 00:08:05.859 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
finished above the top line, and

00:08:05.859 --> 00:08:08.178 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the next day was still above it.

00:08:13.228 --> 00:08:14.681 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Through the top, the sells

00:08:14.681 --> 00:08:16.357 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
have filled and you hold cash.

00:08:16.466 --> 00:08:18.309 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Through the bottom, the buys have

00:08:18.309 --> 00:08:20.153 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled and you hold coin that you

00:08:20.153 --> 00:08:22.164 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bought above where the price is now.

00:08:22.523 --> 00:08:23.976 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That loss can keep growing

00:08:23.976 --> 00:08:25.093 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
until the stop acts.

00:08:25.398 --> 00:08:27.242 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You stop the bot either way, then

00:08:27.242 --> 00:08:28.806 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you follow the written rule.

00:08:28.915 --> 00:08:30.703 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The bot does not decide the stop

00:08:30.703 --> 00:08:32.602 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
unless you turned that setting on.

00:08:32.875 --> 00:08:34.998 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
EXAMPLE, made up: three buys fill

00:08:34.998 --> 00:08:36.794 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on the way down, and you paid

00:08:36.794 --> 00:08:38.917 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
about 800 dollars for that coin.

00:08:39.437 --> 00:08:41.269 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A little below the band

00:08:41.269 --> 00:08:42.908 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it is worth about 720.

00:08:43.428 --> 00:08:45.124 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You are down about 80 dollars

00:08:45.124 --> 00:08:46.891 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
before fees, and the loss keeps

00:08:46.891 --> 00:08:48.587 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
growing until your stop acts.

00:08:49.637 --> 00:08:51.212 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A common mistake is thinking

00:08:51.212 --> 00:08:52.721 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot predicts the price.

00:08:53.509 --> 00:08:54.259 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not.

00:08:54.825 --> 00:08:55.607 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It only waits.

00:08:55.977 --> 00:08:57.486 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Another mistake is starting

00:08:57.486 --> 00:08:58.659 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with no written stop.

00:08:59.074 --> 00:09:00.805 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
There is no promise of results.

00:09:01.202 --> 00:09:02.853 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair card is a teaching

00:09:02.853 --> 00:09:04.054 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sum, marked Example.

00:09:05.104 --> 00:09:07.496 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or demo trading is like driving

00:09:07.496 --> 00:09:09.580 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with L-plates: you practise with

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:12.049 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
pretend money before anything is real.

00:09:12.569 --> 00:09:14.086 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 7 shows you how.

00:09:15.136 --> 00:09:16.824 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This introduction is step one.

00:09:17.524 --> 00:09:18.586 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then what you need.

00:09:19.216 --> 00:09:20.743 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then exactly what a grid

00:09:20.743 --> 00:09:22.194 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bot does, order by order.

00:09:23.194 --> 00:09:24.311 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then market regimes.

00:09:24.887 --> 00:09:26.954 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then choosing grid spacing and range.

00:09:27.593 --> 00:09:29.200 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then entry and exit rules.

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:30.984 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then a paper test.

00:09:31.705 --> 00:09:32.766 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then weekly checks.

00:09:33.503 --> 00:09:34.692 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then common mistakes.

00:09:35.392 --> 00:09:37.403 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then scaling up under written rules.

00:09:37.863 --> 00:09:39.254 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then an opt-in lesson on

00:09:39.254 --> 00:09:41.340 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
liquidation and your complete plan.

00:09:42.406 --> 00:09:43.705 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Steps seven to eleven.

00:09:44.905 --> 00:09:46.805 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The next lesson is a checklist you

00:09:46.805 --> 00:09:48.704 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
write on paper, before any screen.

00:09:49.726 --> 00:09:52.103 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In short: a grid waits, it buys lower and

00:09:52.103 --> 00:09:54.480 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sells higher while price bounces, the

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:56.780 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fees come out of the gap, and if a daily

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:59.233 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close leaves and stays out, you stop the

00:09:59.233 --> 00:10:01.304 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bot and follow the rule you wrote.

00:10:02.388 --> 00:10:03.254 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check yourself.

00:10:03.774 --> 00:10:05.226 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Why does a grid start with

00:10:05.226 --> 00:10:06.679 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
some coin as well as cash?

00:10:06.842 --> 00:10:08.127 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Because the sell orders

00:10:08.127 --> 00:10:09.636 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
need coin you already hold.

00:10:10.653 --> 00:10:12.162 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the example pair, why is

00:10:12.162 --> 00:10:13.838 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the net about eight and a half

00:10:13.838 --> 00:10:15.514 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars and not the whole gap?

00:10:15.944 --> 00:10:17.508 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The two fees come out first.

00:10:18.671 --> 00:10:20.738 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Price closes above your top line, and

00:10:20.738 --> 00:10:22.917 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the next day's close is still above it.

00:10:23.224 --> 00:10:25.012 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
What do you do, and who does it?

00:10:25.332 --> 00:10:27.120 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You stop the bot and follow your

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:28.964 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
written rule, by hand, unless you

00:10:28.964 --> 00:10:30.807 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
turned on the bot's stop setting.

00:10:31.864 --> 00:10:32.614 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Your turn.

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:34.792 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On paper, write the top and the

00:10:34.792 --> 00:10:36.748 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom, one gap, and the stop rule.

00:10:37.851 --> 00:10:39.583 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Say what you will do if a daily

00:10:39.583 --> 00:10:41.203 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close leaves the band and the

00:10:41.203 --> 00:10:42.767 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
next close is still outside.

00:10:43.098 --> 00:10:44.495 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Pause the video and write

00:10:44.495 --> 00:10:46.115 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your answer before you go on.

00:10:47.148 --> 00:10:49.215 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No real order is sent in this lesson.

00:10:49.702 --> 00:10:51.605 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper practice comes in Lesson

00:10:51.605 --> 00:10:53.215 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
7, and real money only after

00:10:53.215 --> 00:10:55.045 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your written graduation rule.

00:10:55.565 --> 00:10:57.572 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A graduation rule is the written

00:10:57.572 --> 00:10:59.281 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
test you pass on paper first.

00:11:00.481 --> 00:11:02.842 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring a notebook, and no secrets: no

00:11:02.842 --> 00:11:05.456 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
seed phrase, private key or API secret.

00:11:05.976 --> 00:11:07.833 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Those are the words or keys that

00:11:07.833 --> 00:11:09.547 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
unlock a wallet or an account.

00:11:10.597 --> 00:11:12.290 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair, in the next lesson,

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:13.905 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is the two things you swap,

00:11:13.905 --> 00:11:15.674 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
like bitcoin and US dollars.

00:11:16.724 --> 00:11:18.557 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid bot places waiting buys

00:11:18.557 --> 00:11:20.610 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
below the price and waiting sells

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.590 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
above it, inside a band you choose.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:24.907 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A finished pair buys

00:11:24.907 --> 00:11:26.192 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lower and sells higher.

00:11:26.399 --> 00:11:28.019 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The fees come out of the gap.

00:11:28.308 --> 00:11:30.487 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the example that was about eight and

00:11:30.487 --> 00:11:32.722 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a half dollars, and it is not a promise.

00:11:33.574 --> 00:11:34.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave through the top and

00:11:34.971 --> 00:11:36.144 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you hold mostly cash.

00:11:36.593 --> 00:11:37.934 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave through the bottom

00:11:37.934 --> 00:11:39.330 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you hold mostly coin.

00:11:40.372 --> 00:11:42.609 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a daily close leaves the band and the

00:11:42.609 --> 00:11:44.707 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
next close is still outside, you stop

00:11:44.707 --> 00:11:46.830 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot and follow the rule you wrote.

00:11:48.004 --> 00:11:50.239 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson: What you are going to need.

00:11:50.628 --> 00:11:52.192 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring your notes: your band,

00:11:52.192 --> 00:11:53.812 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your gaps and your stop rule.

00:11:54.085 --> 00:11:55.443 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep the word Example on

00:11:55.443 --> 00:11:56.733 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every practice figure.

00:11:57.253 --> 00:11:59.208 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson you will write the page

00:11:59.208 --> 00:12:01.219 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of what you need, before any screen.

